# 🤓: Postel's Law = "be conservative in what you send, liberal in what you accept"
# The b00t DWIW extension: when you accept a non-canonical form, tell the agent
# what canonical form was used AND show an example so they can learn.
# This is exactly what deserialize_datum_type warn-once does — but generalizable.

## Problem

# Postel/DWIW in b00t currently means: accept humane input, normalize, execute.
# But agents that send non-canonical input receive no SIGNAL about the canonical form.
# Result: agents repeat the same non-canonical input on every call (no learning).
#
# Current behaviour:
#   `b00t task add "foo" -p P2` → silently normalizes → no feedback
#   `b00t datum filter --types=prd` → silently routes to content-tag → no feedback
#   `@sm0l: foo` (delegation macro) → expands silently → no feedback
#
# Wanted: EACH successful normalization emits a HINT once per session saying:
#   "🔁 normalized 'P2' → priority 2; canonical: `--priority=2`"
#   "🔁 'prd' → content-tag filter; canonical: `b00t datum filter --types=prd`"

## Postel Hint Schema

# A Postel hint is a structured signal attached to the output of any normalization:
#
# ```toml
# [b00t.postel_hint]
# input = "P2"           # what the agent sent
# canonical = "2"        # what b00t normalized to
# example = "b00t task add 'title' --priority=2"   # correct form
# hint = "use 1-4 or P1-P4; critical/high/medium/low also accepted"
# silence = "B00T_POSTEL_HINTS=0"
# ```
#
# In CLI output: shown as `🔁 hint:` prefix, one line, once per (input,canonical) pair.
# In MCP/JSON output: included as `postel_hint` field in JSON response.

## Agent Best Practices Applied

# 1. Helpful hints: every normalization surfaces the canonical form
# 2. Relevant examples: include a complete working command, not just the corrected value
# 3. Silence mechanism: B00T_POSTEL_HINTS=0 for agents in production
# 4. Counted via OTEL: postel_normalizations_total{input_type, canonical_type}
#    Links to PRD-ARCH-009.

## Postel Expansion Points

# | b00t feature | Non-canonical input | Canonical form | Hint already? |
# |---|---|---|---|
# | `--priority` | P2, high, critical | 1-4 | ❌ add |
# | `datum filter --types=prd` | unknown enum string | content-tag | ✅ warn-once |
# | `@sm0l: cmd` delegation | no output-contract | from model-routing.tomllm | ❌ add |
# | `b00t hive run` → guard redirect | find → fdfind | redirect shown | ✅ done |
# | `b00t whoami --role=X` delta load | full reload | delta preferred | ❌ add (PRD-002) |
# | `b00t task done N` | done alias | `task update N --status=completed` | ❌ add |

## Hint Output Format

# CLI (stderr, once per session per (input, canonical) pair):
#   `🔁 b00t: normalized '{input}' → '{canonical}'; example: {example}; silence: B00T_POSTEL_HINTS=0`
#
# JSON (`--json` flag or MCP response):
#   `{ "postel_hint": { "input": "P2", "canonical": "2", "example": "...", "hint": "..." } }`
#
# Silence env: `B00T_POSTEL_HINTS=0` (separate from B00T_DATUM_WARN=0)

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `parse_priority("P2")` emits postel hint once: normalized → 2, example shown
# - [ ] `datum filter --types=prd` (content-tag path) emits postel hint once
# - [ ] Hints are session-scoped: emitted once per (input, canonical) pair per process
# - [ ] JSON output mode: postel_hint in response body
# - [ ] B00T_POSTEL_HINTS=0 silences all hints
# - [ ] OTEL counter: postel_normalizations_total incremented (links PRD-ARCH-009)

